  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21791810",
      "title": "Vue 3: New Features",
      "lectureOrder": 328,
      "videoOrder": 293,
      "sourceHash": "d2e8a686b1c45a8c61d18a522e69ff707f5ffc4643f82c620aed1d20c6a8928b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "Now that's it for the changes that you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 7.75,
          "en": "Now let's dive into the new features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.75,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "Here we got a teleport component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 12.32,
          "en": "and a feature called fragments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.32,
          "end": 13.903,
          "en": "Now what's that all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 16.84,
          "en": "Again, I prepared something for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.84,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "The teleport fragments folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 20.823,
          "en": "Let's dive into that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.49,
          "end": 26.473,
          "en": "And NPM install and NPM run serve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.7,
          "end": 31.02,
          "en": "Once this is up and running. If I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 33.38,
          "en": "that is what I got. And if I click on a button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.38,
          "end": 36.23,
          "en": "I get this modal where I can confirm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.23,
          "end": 38.47,
          "en": "that I want to deactivate this or cancel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.47,
          "end": 39.85,
          "en": "And if I confirm it's gone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.85,
          "end": 42.913,
          "en": "so a very simple dummy app here, using Vue 3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.79,
          "end": 46.06,
          "en": "Now, here we can use two new features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.06,
          "end": 48.943,
          "en": "teleport and fragments. Let's start with teleport.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.82,
          "end": 51.85,
          "en": "If I opened this modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.85,
          "end": 55.34,
          "en": "we can inspect this in the dev tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.34,
          "end": 57.393,
          "en": "And here in the elements tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.52,
          "end": 62.28,
          "en": "we actually see that this dialogue and the backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.28,
          "end": 66.92,
          "en": "is rendered somewhere nested in our element tree, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.92,
          "end": 69.07,
          "en": "So this is the real DOM and our backdrop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.07,
          "end": 71.603,
          "en": "and dialogue is deeply nested in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.51,
          "end": 75.41,
          "en": "Now, visually that's no problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.41,
          "end": 79.15,
          "en": "but it's actually not perfect for semantics",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.15,
          "end": 80.82,
          "en": "for accessibility, maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.82,
          "end": 82.78,
          "en": "And it could even break your styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.78,
          "end": 85.82,
          "en": "if you don't work with set index, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.82,
          "end": 89.53,
          "en": "In general, this of course should be an overlay to the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.53,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "So logically it should not be deeply nested in the DOM tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 97.31,
          "en": "Instead, it should be directly inside of the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.31,
          "end": 99.03999999999999,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.03999999999999,
          "end": 101.45,
          "en": "Now this is not something you technically need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.45,
          "end": 104.62,
          "en": "but it's simply would be a bit better logically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.62,
          "end": 107.4,
          "en": "semantically, from accessibility perspectives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.4,
          "end": 110.14,
          "en": "And hence, it would be great if we could move this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.14,
          "end": 112.59,
          "en": "and the dialogue to a different place in the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.47,
          "end": 116.21000000000001,
          "en": "With Vue 2 this wasn't really possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.21000000000001,
          "end": 118.07,
          "en": "with Vue 3 it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.07,
          "end": 120.34,
          "en": "We now got a feature called teleport.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.34,
          "end": 123.423,
          "en": "If you know, react there, it's called portal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.32,
          "end": 125.89,
          "en": "Now, how does it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.89,
          "end": 129.13,
          "en": "In the component where you want to move things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.13,
          "end": 132.1,
          "en": "for example, here in the confirmed dialogue component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.1,
          "end": 137.1,
          "en": "you can simply wrap your entire component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.38,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "your entire template with a new built in teleport component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.73,
          "end": 144.82999999999998,
          "en": "just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.82999999999998,
          "end": 147.91,
          "en": "And then on teleport, you need the to prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.91,
          "end": 150.98,
          "en": "where you pass in a CSS selector, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.98,
          "end": 153.25,
          "en": "selecting the body element to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.25,
          "end": 156.1,
          "en": "that everything in here should actually be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.1,
          "end": 158.32,
          "en": "directly in the body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.32,
          "end": 161.43,
          "en": "Now you still use this component as you did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.43,
          "end": 163.78,
          "en": "So I can still use it in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.78,
          "end": 165.94,
          "en": "of another nested component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.94,
          "end": 170.21,
          "en": "As I'm doing here in admin mode, this is still possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.21,
          "end": 174.26,
          "en": "We can still pass props to this component, listen to events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.26,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "This all works as you learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.61,
          "end": 179.38,
          "en": "But now the actual DOM, which has rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.38,
          "end": 182.09,
          "en": "will be rendered in a different place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.09,
          "end": 187.09,
          "en": "If we save that and reload, I can still view this modal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.32,
          "end": 191.4,
          "en": "but if we now inspect it, we see this div, the backdrop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.4,
          "end": 193.86,
          "en": "the dialogue and the div which holds both",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.86,
          "end": 195.84,
          "en": "that's now directly in the body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 199.67000000000002,
          "en": "It's not deeply nested in our arbor component tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.67000000000002,
          "end": 202.64,
          "en": "in our arbor node tree, I should say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.64,
          "end": 205.45,
          "en": "So that's teleport a nice new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.45,
          "end": 207.29,
          "en": "which allows you to write semantically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.29,
          "end": 209.853,
          "en": "more correct HTML code, I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.32999999999998,
          "end": 214.44,
          "en": "Another nice feature is the fragment feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 214.44,
          "end": 217.4,
          "en": "Here in admin mode, I got this confirmed dialogue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.4,
          "end": 218.98,
          "en": "inside of this list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.98,
          "end": 221.03,
          "en": "Now, technically I can place it anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.03,
          "end": 222.5,
          "en": "because we just learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.5,
          "end": 225.51,
          "en": "that the HTML code will be rendered somewhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.51,
          "end": 227.26,
          "en": "But still to make it clear that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.26,
          "end": 229.32999999999998,
          "en": "this is not really in the list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.32999999999998,
          "end": 231.76,
          "en": "It just belongs to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.76,
          "end": 234.1,
          "en": "We might want to move it out of there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.1,
          "end": 236.48,
          "en": "And with Vue 2 this was not allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 236.48,
          "end": 238.88,
          "en": "My IDE still gives me an error here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.88,
          "end": 242.25,
          "en": "but I can tell you with Vue 3, this is allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.25,
          "end": 246.95,
          "en": "With Vue 3 you may have multiple root elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 246.95,
          "end": 249.19,
          "en": "inside of your component template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 249.19,
          "end": 252.01,
          "en": "You're not restricted to have just one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 252.01,
          "end": 254.29,
          "en": "You can have multiple sibling elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 254.29,
          "end": 256.16,
          "en": "directly in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 256.16,
          "end": 257.08,
          "en": "This is new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 257.08,
          "end": 261.23,
          "en": "This was not supported with Vue 2, now with Vue 3,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.23,
          "end": 265.003,
          "en": "this works, as you can tell, we got no error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 268.31,
          "en": "And that's teleport and fragments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 268.31,
          "end": 270.05,
          "en": "Now the biggest new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 270.05,
          "end": 274.4,
          "en": "which is 100% optional is the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 274.4,
          "end": 279.31,
          "en": "The composition API can replace the existing options API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 279.31,
          "end": 281.64,
          "en": "And I actually want to take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 281.64,
          "end": 284.85,
          "en": "at this composition API, therefore I have this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 284.85,
          "end": 287.78,
          "en": "in a separate lecture right after this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 287.78,
          "end": 290.34000000000003,
          "en": "Before we go to that separate video though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 290.34000000000003,
          "end": 292.97,
          "en": "here's the last new feature I wanna touch on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 292.97,
          "end": 295.56,
          "en": "It's kind of new TypeScript support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 295.56,
          "end": 298.6,
          "en": "You always could use TypeScript with Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.6,
          "end": 302.83,
          "en": "with Vue 3, it's now easier because Vue 3 internally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.83,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "is built with TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 306.6,
          "en": "Now, if you wanna learn more about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 306.6,
          "end": 308.67,
          "en": "I recommend the official docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 308.67,
          "end": 311.42,
          "en": "There, you can learn all about TypeScript support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 311.42,
          "end": 314.59,
          "en": "and how to use TypeScript in your Vue 3 projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.59,
          "end": 316.98,
          "en": "and how to write TypeScript code there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 316.98,
          "end": 320.19,
          "en": "It's an alternative. You don't have to use TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 320.19,
          "end": 322.84,
          "en": "I'm using Java script in most of my projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 322.84,
          "end": 325.543,
          "en": "but you can use TypeScript if you prefer that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
